body:
I've changed the name of this issue (originally just about "reserving" the `Polyform-` prefix) so that it is more precisely about the request to add the Polyform licenses to the list.

@kemitchell has submitted a PR at #903 

As mentioned above, I think the primary gating item here is the pending update to the license inclusion principles per #925. I expect the outcome of those changes will be the precursor to adding these to the list.

@kemitchell - based on this thread alone, I'm not sure I can see how the accusation against @richardfontana holds water.  I can guess that you both have some history here but let's try to leave that out, ok?

I appreciate that you are trying to design for and consider the use of SPDX identifiers in advance. That being said, you are probably a bit biased as to whether the licenses are "meaningful" (understandably)

One prior example to consider: SSPL (a license that had a certain about of "political activity" around it) was added to the SPDX License List, but not right away. A main reason for adding it was the need for being able to identify it - when it was found by scanners for example or by others. It was not the license authors who asked for it to be added (although, we did let them know, a practice that has been helpful)

@pombredanne, @swinslow reserved the `Polyform-` prefix for us in the standard namespace [above](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/885#issuecomment-519612576).

Our primary motive for submission was to give project maintainers the ability to express their license choices in package metadata and other places where SPDX IDs or expressions are required or supported. I'm interested in the namespaces work as a general SPDX contributor. But I'm not aware of any packaging system supporting it.

Discussion here has gone from [expecting the new license inclusion principles to clear the way for landing the PR](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/885#issuecomment-569955840) to [wielding the very guidelines these licenses partially prompted against it](https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/885#issuecomment-610474483). I'd like to work through that, one way or another, not dodge it.

@pombredanne @kemitchell - I think we need to be clear on the order of ask and answers here:
1) The Polyform licenses have been requested to be added on the SPDX License List  - we need to answer that question first.
2) IF the answer to that question is no, then the suggestion for use of the namespace option is a great one and the obvious next step.

@pombredanne - I wanted to clarify that because by mentioning the namespace option, one could infer that you are saying you don't think the Polyform licenses should be added to the SPDX License List. But I'm not sure if that was your intention? Would appreciate hearing your thoughts as to that question.

We need to answer that question first: it's not an easy one, especially given we are answering it for not 1, but 5 licenses at once. But it's also a good test of the new license inclusion guidelines!
